          <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400" data-i18n="faqSubtitle">Clear answers to common questions about Image to URL conversion.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-3" id="faq-accordion">
          <!-- FAQ 1 -->
          <div class="bg-dark-surface border border-dark-border rounded-2xl p-4 cursor-pointer faq-item hover:border-cyan-500/40 transition">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200" data-i18n="faq1Q">How to get Image Url from file?</h4>
              <i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 transition-transform duration-200 faq-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-content hidden mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-dark-border text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed" data-i18n="faq1A">To get an Image URL from a file, simply drag and drop your image file into our converter, or click &quot;Browse Files&quot; to select it from your device. Our tool instantly reads your file locally using the browser&#x27;s FileReader API and encodes it into a standard Data URL (e.g., data:image/png;base64,...) or provides ready-to-copy HTML, Markdown, and direct embed links. You can copy the generated URL immediately with one click.</div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 2 -->
          <div class="bg-dark-surface border border-dark-border rounded-2xl p-4 cursor-pointer faq-item hover:border-cyan-500/40 transition">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200" data-i18n="faq2Q">How to make a Url for an Image?</h4>
              <i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 transition-transform duration-200 faq-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-content hidden mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-dark-border text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed" data-i18n="faq2A">Making a URL for an image is easy: upload your image into our online converter by dragging your file or pasting it from your clipboard (Ctrl + V). The converter automatically transforms the raw image into a Data URL or embed link. You can then copy the resulting URL to use in web pages, CSS stylesheets, README markdown files, or email newsletters without requiring an external web host.</div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 3 -->
          <div class="bg-dark-surface border border-dark-border rounded-2xl p-4 cursor-pointer faq-item hover:border-cyan-500/40 transition">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200" data-i18n="faq3Q">How to convert Image to Url?</h4>
              <i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 transition-transform duration-200 faq-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-content hidden mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-dark-border text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed" data-i18n="faq3A">To convert an image to a URL, drop your image (PNG, JPG, WebP, SVG, or GIF) into our conversion tool. The tool instantly converts the image into an RFC 2397 Data URL string, HTML &lt;img&gt; embed tag, CSS background URL, and Markdown link. You can customize output dimensions and compression quality before copying your direct URL.</div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 4 -->
          <div class="bg-dark-surface border border-dark-border rounded-2xl p-4 cursor-pointer faq-item hover:border-cyan-500/40 transition">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200" data-i18n="faq4Q">How to convert Image to Link?</h4>
              <i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 transition-transform duration-200 faq-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-content hidden mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-dark-border text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed" data-i18n="faq4A">Converting an image to a link involves encoding the graphic data into a web-accessible address format. With our free in-browser converter, you upload the image, select your desired link format (such as direct Data URI, HTML snippet, Markdown link, or BBCode), and click &quot;Copy&quot;. You can also generate a mobile-scannable QR code link to share the image across devices effortlessly.</div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 5 -->
          <div class="bg-dark-surface border border-dark-border rounded-2xl p-4 cursor-pointer faq-item hover:border-cyan-500/40 transition">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200" data-i18n="faq5Q">What is an Image to Data URL converter?</h4>
              <i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 transition-transform duration-200 faq-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-content hidden mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-dark-border text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed" data-i18n="faq5A">An Image to Data URL converter is a software utility that transforms binary image files into an ASCII-encoded Base64 string formatted as a Data Uniform Resource Identifier (data:image/...;base64,...). This enables images to be embedded directly into HTML documents, CSS files, and Markdown pages without sending a separate HTTP request to an external image hosting server.</div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 6 -->
          <div class="bg-dark-surface border border-dark-border rounded-2xl p-4 cursor-pointer faq-item hover:border-cyan-500/40 transition">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200" data-i18n="faq6Q">Are my images saved on any external servers?</h4>
              <i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 transition-transform duration-200 faq-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-content hidden mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-dark-border text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed" data-i18n="faq6A">No. 100% of the image processing, encoding, compression, and QR code generation occurs strictly inside your web browser&#x27;s local sandbox. No files, logs, or personal data ever leave your computer.</div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 7 -->
          <div class="bg-dark-surface border border-dark-border rounded-2xl p-4 cursor-pointer faq-item hover:border-cyan-500/40 transition">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200" data-i18n="faq7Q">Can I convert transparent PNGs without losing transparency?</h4>
              <i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 transition-transform duration-200 faq-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-content hidden mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-dark-border text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed" data-i18n="faq7A">Yes! Our dedicated PNG to URL tool preserves the full 32-bit alpha channel, ensuring your logos and icons remain perfectly transparent when embedded.</div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 8 -->
          <div class="bg-dark-surface border border-dark-border rounded-2xl p-4 cursor-pointer faq-item hover:border-cyan-500/40 transition">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200" data-i18n="faq8Q">What is the difference between Data URL and Hosted URL?</h4>
              <i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 transition-transform duration-200 faq-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-content hidden mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-dark-border text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed" data-i18n="faq8A">A Data URL embeds the complete image data inline (e.g. data:image/png;base64,...), which never expires and works offline. A Hosted URL points to an external web location or CDN endpoint.</div>
          </div>

          <!-- FAQ 9 -->
          <div class="bg-dark-surface border border-dark-border rounded-2xl p-4 cursor-pointer faq-item hover:border-cyan-500/40 transition">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-200" data-i18n="faq9Q">Can I decode a Base64 string back into an image file?</h4>
              <i data-lucide="chevron-down" class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 transition-transform duration-200 faq-icon"></i>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-content hidden mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-dark-border text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed" data-i18n="faq9A">Yes, use our built-in Base64 to Image tool from the Tools menu. Paste your Base64 or Data URI string to view dimensions and download the image file directly to your desktop.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
